Day 1 — AWS EC2 + Autoscaling + Load Balancing

Scenario-Based DevOps Interview Questions

1️⃣ Your EC2 instances experience high CPU during peak hours but remain idle overnight. How will you design an Auto Scaling strategy with scheduled + dynamic scaling?

2️⃣ You need zero-downtime deployment for an EC2-based web app. How will you design this using Launch Templates + ASG + ALB?

3️⃣ An EC2 instance in a private subnet needs to download OS patches. What AWS components will you configure?

4️⃣ Your application requires session stickiness for user logins. How will you configure stickiness on ALB or NLB?

5️⃣ ASG scales out, but new instances fail health checks immediately. What will you check during troubleshooting?

6️⃣ A workload needs GPUs for ML inference. How will you choose instance family, optimize cost, and configure placement groups?

7️⃣ A critical VM crash caused data loss on an attached instance store. Which storage architecture should you choose instead?

8️⃣ You must migrate 150 on-prem VMs to AWS with minimal downtime. Which AWS service will you use and how will you plan cutover?

9️⃣ EC2 boot time is slow due to lengthy startup scripts. How will you optimize AMIs, user data, and configuration?

🔟 Network traffic between two EC2 instances in different AZs is slow. What network-level factors will you analyze?

1️⃣1️⃣ You need encrypted volumes, automatic snapshots, and cross-region DR. How will you design EBS strategy?

1️⃣2️⃣ You want to isolate workload groups at the hardware level. When will you choose Dedicated Hosts or Dedicated Instances?

1️⃣3️⃣ A legacy app needs static public IP even after instance replacement. What AWS features will you use?

1️⃣4️⃣ Your ASG is scaling in aggressively and terminating instances too early. How will you tune cooldowns and lifecycle hooks?

1️⃣5️⃣ A new version rollout introduced bugs. How will you roll back safely in an EC2-based architecture?

